<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Few showers seen over parts of S.Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Few showers seen over parts of S.Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department forecast scattered showers at several places in the Western and Sabaragamuwa provinces and in Galle, Matara and Kurunegala districts for Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement on Tuesday that gusts of fairly strong winds will continue to prevail along the western slopes of the central hills during showers on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Monday morning:</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		    7.5</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    17.0</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   1.0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		  2.0</p>
<p>    Moussakele		7.6</p>
<p>    Norton		    8.0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
